    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0198" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/2508: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-01T09:00:00+01:00">May 1, 1940—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 1—6:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>551. The Belgian Ambassador<anchor n="49b" xml:id="d128-f1"/> said to me last
                    night that his Government had now made it entirely clear to the German
                    Government that if German troops should enter the Netherlands Belgium would
                    march in support of the Netherlands immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
